Doctor incorrectly uses CRLF (
) instead of LF (
) line terminator. When playing around with Doctor it was noticed that Doctor changes a unix file (LF) into CRLF. Doctor should never modify the original line endings of a file. It should use what format the file already was. Way to test from Beuc: Here's our test: - reed create index.html using cvs - I update index.html using Doctor - index.html had 
